                <pb facs="0502" n="422" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg422"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Merry.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-09-17"><hi rendition="#italic">September 17,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In the name of President Roosevelt and the American nation you will assure
                    President Iglesias of deep appreciation of his messages of solicitude and
                    sympathy in the hour of suspense and affliction.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
